text.section:
A trust may be created by:

Transfer of property to another person as trustee during the settlor's lifetime by the settlor or by the settlor's agent, acting in accordance with § 64.2-1612, under a power of attorney that expressly authorizes the agent to create a trust on the settlor's behalf or by will or other disposition taking effect upon the settlor's death;


Declaration by the owner of property that the owner holds identifiable property as trustee;


Exercise of a power of appointment in favor of a trustee; or


A conservator acting in accordance with § 64.2-2023.
